    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (81.25) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) serving as our undisputed pillars of production. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.454 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns his high rating through a potent combination of a 14% park boost and a significant 19% SP skill advantage against Tomoyuki Sugano. **Christian Yelich** (68.09) also projects as an elite start, buoyed by an ideal leadoff spot and a 13% platoon-based efficiency bump. While **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** draw tough matchups against Dylan Cease, their roles at the top of the lineup keep them as necessary staples despite the downward pressure from Cease\u2019s SP skill.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Lars Nootbaar** (51.12) out of the active roster. Despite an elite 0.406 xwOBA and a positive platoon edge against Freddy Peralta, he failed to surpass the marginal efficiency of **Kazuma Okamoto** (43.02) and the rest of the utility contingent, ultimately falling victim to a lack of upside compared to our prioritized baserunners. Looking ahead, we remain cautious regarding the rain risk in the Tampa Bay matchup; both **Dillon Dingler** (43.58) and **Colt Keith** (57.67) are at risk of a postponement, which would force us to pivot toward the bench depth represented by **Nelson Velazquez** or **Chase Meidroth**. Beyond weather, keep a close watch on the official lineups for **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, and **Caleb Durbin**; their current projections are predicated on assumed spots, and any move down the order could render them below-floor options for today's 5x5 rotation.",
